\f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super $}{ InfoBoxes}}#{\footnote \pard\plain \s121\ql \li120\ri0\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super 
#}{ InfoBoxes}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s121\ql \li120\ri0\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super K}{ InfoBoxes}}}{\fs20 InfoBoxes
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li120\ri0\sa60\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Inf
oBoxes are rectangular regions of the display which can contain simple text, reports, bitmaps and data from attribute files. The InfoBox has an optional pointer from the box to a location in the display to which it is tied. While the InfoBox can be easily
 moved to any desired location, the head of the pointer remains fixed to the tie point.
\par 
\par An InfoBox consists of a text field, an associated attribute file and a set of display characteristics. The text field can be up to 1024 characters and be any valid Geo
Master expression. Two special instances of the text field are also recognized; the $BITMAP function and the $REPORT function.
\par 
\par InfoBoxes are stored in the configuration file if the Save InfoBoxes option is used when saving the configuration file. They may also be saved to an external file (ending in the .inb extension) and latter recalled when needed.
\par 
\par InfoBoxes are created either interactively using  the GF_CREATE_INFOBOX command or in a macro using the }{\uldb $INFOBOX }{\v d}{\v\cf13 f_}{\v infobox }{function. Once created, they can
 be moved using the GF_MOVE_INFOBOX command and modified and deleted using the GF_EDIT_INFOBOX command. 
\par 
\par By use of the InfoBox Contents field, predefined InfoBox templates may be automatically selected based on the type of graphic element selected by the user. By use of the }{\uldb InfoBox Name field}{\v\cf13 infobox_names}{
, several InfoBoxes can share the same characteristics and changes made to one can be automatically applied to others.
\par }{\b \page }{\cs117\b\super *{\footnote \pard\plain \s121\ql \li120\ri0\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super *}{ IDM_INFOBOXNAME}}${\footnote \pard\plain 
\s121\ql \li120\ri0\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super $}{ Using the InfoBox Name Field}}#{\footnote \pard\plain \s121\ql \li120\ri0\sl-220\slmult0
\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super #}{ infobox_names}}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s121\ql \li120\ri0\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 
\f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super K}{ InfoBoxes;InfoBoxes,Names;}}}{Using the InfoBox Name Field
\par 
\par The infobox name field uniquely identifies an infobox. It is made up of a group field and an optional instance field in the format  group:instance. It can be up to 32 characters long. For example, the following are valid infobox names:
\par 
\par \tab }{\cs119\f2 TAXINFO:1
\par \tab TAXINFO:2
\par \tab BUILDINGDATA:1
\par \tab TITLEBOX}{
\par 
\par The first three contain both the group and inst
ance fields, the last contains only the group field. All infoboxes currently loaded which share the same group identifier share the same display characteristics. Changing the display characteristics of one instance of a group changes the same characterist
ic for all instances of that group. For example, changing the font size for the second infobox above (instance 2 of the TAXINFO group) also changes the font size of the first infobox.
\par 
\par When you create a new infobox, GeoMaster automatically adds a colon and 
number to the end of the current name or, if the current name ends in a number, increments it to the next number. You can override the automatically supplied name by typing in any name you desire. 
\par 
\par Selecting the pull-down icon to the right of the name all
ows you to do one of two things, depending on the status of the edit checkbox to the right of the name. If the edit checkbox is checked, selecting a name from the name list will save any changes to the current infobox and switch to the selected infobox. A
n
y further edits will be applied to this infobox. If the edit checkbox is not checked, selecting a name from the list will copy the display characteristics from the selected infobox to the current one. The name of the current infobox will change to the nex
t available instance of the selected infobox.
\par \page }{\cs117\super ${\footnote \pard\plain \s121\ql \li120\ri0\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin120\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs117\super $}{ The Theme Legend}}#{\footnote \pard\plain 
